{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_mcp_tools", "label": "ABAP ADT MCP Server - Complete Tool Reference (MCP-Tools.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_sap_adt_http_api", "label": "SAP ABAP Development Tools (ADT) HTTP API (/sap/bc/adt)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_abap_adt_api", "label": "abap-adt-api client library", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_sap_gateway_json_rpc_service", "label": "SAP Gateway JSON-RPC 2.0 service (/sap/gw/jsonrpc)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_tool_profiles", "label": "Tool profiles (core / analyst / dev / all)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ABAP_MCP_PROFILE limits what tools/list returns to cut the per-turn schema cost (core ~2.7k tokens vs all ~17.8k). A tool outside the profile is neither listed nor callable, and the error says so, so callers do not retry. core is 9 rather than 12 because editAbapSource replaced the four stepwise write tools."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_response_budget", "label": "Per-profile response size ceiling (status:truncated)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An over-budget answer comes back as valid JSON with a 2,000-byte preview and a nextStep instead of a cut-off fragment. Retrying the identical call gives the identical refusal, so the caller has to narrow the request with a filter, a name or a row limit."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_tooldefinition_contract", "label": "ToolDefinition contract (inputSchema, narrowingHint, needsFeature)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is no optional:true flag because it was never JSON Schema; required is the only optionality marker. Arguments are still not schema-validated at the door, so handlers validate what they can."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_tool_annotations", "label": "MCP tool annotations (readOnly / destructive / idempotent / openWorld hints)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The hints let a client auto-approve the 82 read-only tools and prompt on the rest. They are not a permission system. Each tool declares them next to its name, so a rename cannot silently drop them. All four flags are always stated because OpenAI's tool directory rejects omissions, and client defaults would read a missing destructiveHint as true."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_basehandler", "label": "BaseHandler execution layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_request_lifecycle", "label": "Request lifecycle and routing table derived from getTools()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deriving the routing table from getTools() means a tool cannot be listed without being callable. Duplicate names are refused at startup, and TOOL_ALIASES keeps renamed tools callable without listing them."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_authentication_modes", "label": "Authentication modes (Kerberos, X.509, OAuth, password - never Basic with placeholder)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The heuristics prefer credentials that cannot lock a SAP user. The placeholder password is never sent, so Basic attempts cannot lock a technical user. The credential is presented once and the session cookie carries the rest, so a short-lived OAuth token is not a problem."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_sso_session_bootstrap", "label": "SSO session bootstrap and injection (bootstrapSsoSession / injectSsoSession)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kerberos shells out to curl --negotiate because Node cannot do SPNEGO. Injecting the SAP_SESSIONID cookies and the CSRF token flips AdtHTTP to logged-in, so it never Basic-auths with the placeholder."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_server_self_documentation", "label": "Server self-documentation (MCP resources, readServerGuide, readSkill)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resources are usually attached by the user, so an agent will not discover them on its own, but a tool is already in its context. Reading a whole guide is opt-in (index ~6 kB, one section ~1.5 kB) to save tokens. Skills are discovered from disk on every call."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_system_identity", "label": "System identity binding (SAP_SYSTEM_ID declared vs observed)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is one server per system and client. The id observed in the session cookie beats the declared one. A mismatch warns rather than refusing to start, because the damage comes from routing, not execution, and failing hard would brick a server after a system copy or rename."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_adt_uris", "label": "ADT object URL vs source URL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_locks", "label": "Locks bound to the stateful session", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "dropSession or a restart invalidates lock handles. Always unlock, including on failure paths, because a stranded lock blocks the object for other users."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_transports", "label": "Transport request handling ($TMP vs transportable objects)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_positions", "label": "ADT positions (1-based line, 0-based column)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_object_versions", "label": "Object versions (active / inactive / workingArea)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_objects_go_in_as_objects", "label": "Objects-go-in-as-objects rule for multi-step flows", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tools that continue a flow (unitTestEvaluation, fixEdits, renamePreview, pushRepo, atcRequestExemption) take the object returned by the previous call unchanged. Passing a name string fails."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_golden_paths", "label": "Golden paths (copy-pasteable workflows)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_write_cycle", "label": "Write cycle: lock -> setObjectSource -> unLock -> activateByName", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SAP refuses to activate an object its own editor still holds ('User is currently editing'). The order the document used to prescribe, lock -> write -> activate -> unlock, failed at the activation every time; verified on DEV/100."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_new_object_by_url", "label": "Fill a newly created object by objectUrl, not by name", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A new object stays inactive until its first activation, and the repository search only knows active objects, so resolving it by name reports that it was not found."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_srfc_callability_check", "label": "SRFC package node as cheap RFC-callability check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RFC_GET_FUNCTION_INTERFACE reads any function module's signature, RFC-enabled or not, so a successful readAbapFunctionModule is documentation, not proof the module is callable. The SRFC node lists the RFC-enabled modules without calling one."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_vclient_override_trap", "label": "Per-port VCLIENT overrides global icm/HTTPS/verify_client", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_json_rpc_protocol_facts", "label": "JSON-RPC protocol facts (/IWBEP/CL_JSRPC_*)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unmatched or lower-case parameter keys are dropped silently. Calls therefore go through callFunctionViaJsonRpc, which upper-cases the keys and validates them against the real signature."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_one_luw_batch", "label": "One-LUW batch for an update BAPI and its commit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The members of a JSON-RPC array request run in one ABAP session and roll area. Separate calls land in different LUWs, so the BAPI's changes are lost. Verified live with an insert, a read-back and a rollback in one batch."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_one_path_design_decision", "label": "Design decision: one code path for one or many RFC calls (runCalls / invokeJsonRpcBatch)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything above the transport is count-agnostic. Only the wire format branches (object vs array), because the SAP processor branches on it. That leaves the single-call behaviour verified on DEV/100 untouched."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_json_rpc_error_map", "label": "JSON-RPC error map (-32601, -32600/-32602, -31000)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_response_error_model", "label": "Response and error model (single-level MCP envelope, handleError)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_stderr_logging", "label": "Never log to stdout - stderr-only logger", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The server speaks MCP over stdio, so a stray console.log in a handler corrupts the protocol stream for every tool."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_healthcheck", "label": "healthcheck tool (profile, system identity, reachability layers)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_troubleshooting_matrix", "label": "Troubleshooting matrix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_test_suites", "label": "Offline test suites (handlerContract, toolDefinitions, jsonRpcHandlers, ...)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The suites run against fakes of ADTClient, so they prove the wrapper contract (argument mapping, envelopes, error translation), not how any ADT endpoint behaves."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_tools_extending_the_server", "label": "Extending the server (one-file tool addition)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_sap_adt_http_api", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_abap_adt_api", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_sap_gateway_json_rpc_service", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_tool_profiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_response_budget", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_tooldefinition_contract", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_tool_annotations", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_basehandler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/MCP-Tools.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_mcp_tools", "target": "docs_mcp_tools_request_lifecycle", "rel